---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PostHeader from "@dario-loi/polytope/astro/PostHeader.astro";
import { analytics, person } from "../site";
const on = Boolean(analytics.websiteId);
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="How this site counts visits in aggregate with Umami, and the one setting your browser keeps." crumbs={[{ name: person.name, href: "/" }, { name: "Privacy", href: "/privacy/" }]}>
  <div class="ply-container">
    <PostHeader title="Privacy" stop lede="I count visits to this site in aggregate. It shows me which pages people find useful." />
  </div>
  <hr class="ply-rule" />
  <div class="ply-container privacy">
    <div class="ply-prose">
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>{on ? "Visits are counted anonymously with" : "When analytics is enabled, visits are counted anonymously with"} <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami</a>, a privacy-friendly analytics service. Your IP address is used only to estimate a rough location. It is then discarded. I can also see which links and interactive figures people use. Page load times come through too. Both tell me what to fix.</p>
      <h2>Search</h2>
      <p>Search runs in your browser on an index it downloads from this site. The words you type stay on your device. I see that a search happened, roughly how many results it found, and which kind of page was opened.</p>
      <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p>If you switch between light and dark themes, your browser remembers the choice. The next page then opens the same way. That setting stays on your device.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>I only read the numbers in aggregate. If you have questions, use the email link in the footer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .privacy { padding-top: var(--ply-space-6); }
</style>
